---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { voiceTurn as turn } from '../showcases/voice-turn/content';
---
<section class="voice-turn-showcase wrap" id="recorded-voice-turn" aria-labelledby="voice-turn-heading" data-recorded-voice-turn>
  <div class="voice-turn-intro">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">One recorded voice turn</p><h2 id="voice-turn-heading">A recorded request.<br /><em>A spoken reply.</em></h2></div>
    <p>Actual PanelForge voice components and server pipeline in an isolated wrapper. Stock file-backed input, real provider responses, and a muted recording.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="voice-turn-static">These are saved clips. Playing them opens no microphone and sends no speech.</p>
  <div class="voice-turn-clips">
    <article aria-labelledby="voice-request-title">
      <p class="voice-turn-label">01 / Recorded request</p><h3 id="voice-request-title">An imaginary moon garden</h3>
      <p class="voice-turn-origin" id="voice-request-origin">Stock machine voice, captured by the browser’s recorder. Fictional request.</p>
      <audio controls preload="none" aria-label="Recorded request audio" aria-describedby="voice-request-origin" data-voice-input><source src={`${turn.media}/recorded-request.wav`} type="audio/wav" /><a href={`${turn.media}/recorded-request.wav`}>Open the recorded request audio</a></audio>
      <p class="voice-turn-transcript-label">Recognized speech</p><blockquote>{turn.recognized}</blockquote>
    </article>
    <article aria-labelledby="voice-reply-title">
      <p class="voice-turn-label">02 / Saved reply</p><h3 id="voice-reply-title">{turn.reply}</h3>
      <p class="voice-turn-origin" id="voice-reply-origin">OpenAI generated speech · <code>tts-1</code> · Alloy voice.</p>
      <audio controls preload="none" aria-label="Generated reply audio" aria-describedby="voice-reply-origin" data-voice-reply><source src={`${turn.media}/reply.wav`} type="audio/wav" /><a href={`${turn.media}/reply.wav`}>Open the generated reply audio</a></audio>
      <p class="voice-turn-transcript-label">What was saved</p><p class="voice-turn-result">One recognized request, one saved answer, and one returned audio chunk played to completion by the canonical queue.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="voice-turn-path">Groq transcribed the recording; Haiku answered through Claude Engine; OpenAI synthesized the reply.</p>
  <details class="voice-turn-disclosure" data-voice-film><summary>Watch the recorded component flow <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
    <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster={`${turn.media}/component-flow.webp`} width="1280" height="900" aria-label="Recorded PanelForge voice component flow" aria-describedby="voice-film-scope" data-voice-video><source src={`${turn.media}/component-flow.mp4`} type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src={`${turn.media}/component-flow.vtt`} srclang="en" label="English action captions" default /><p><a href={`${turn.media}/component-flow.mp4`}>Open the silent component recording</a></p></video><figcaption id="voice-film-scope">Continuous 20.88-second recording of the isolated component wrapper, including the real waits. The original browser output was muted. Its player’s completion events establish playback progression, not that a person heard speakers. The lower edge of the final reply is clipped in the capture; the exact saved text is readable above.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="voice-turn-links"><a href={`${turn.media}/component-flow.mp4`}>Open the film full size <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><a href={`${turn.media}/component-flow.vtt`}>Read the action captions <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div>
  </div></details>
  <details class="voice-turn-disclosure" data-voice-method><summary>Source, method and limits <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div class="voice-turn-method">
    <p>The input began as fictional eSpeak stock speech supplied to Chromium’s file-backed device. The browser recorded a new WebM/Opus file and uploaded it to the actual transcription route. The listening clip above is decoded and resampled from that upload to mono 24 kHz PCM WAV, with no cuts, speed change or volume normalization. Its converted bytes differ from the uploaded recording. The reply WAV preserves the exact generated and persisted bytes.</p>
    <p>The observed model was <code>{turn.model}</code> through Claude Engine and Claude CLI <code>{turn.cli}</code>. The turn used Groq Whisper transcription and OpenAI <code>tts-1</code> with Alloy speech. Exactly one PTT submission led to one observed Groq response, one SDK model turn and one observed OpenAI speech response. Model turns are not an inferred count of Anthropic HTTP requests or billed calls.</p>
    <p>The private runtime used an empty SDK toolset, an explicit deny-all tool hook, one SDK turn, a $0.50 model budget, a configured 160-token output cap and an independent 240-second stop. The custom wrapper, isolated user/session/database/storage and intercepted queued jobs, broadcasts, notifications and mail are test substitutions. The normal voice policy stayed in place. No production writes or production application runtime use occurred.</p>
    <p>The actual queue received and completed one final chunk, index zero. The separate three-note example below tests local multi-item ordering. Neither this file-backed recording nor the saved audio establishes a physical microphone, human audibility, digital output capture, device routing or Safari/iOS behavior.</p>
    <p>Source snapshots: PanelForge <code>93881d2</code> / <code>web-v10.20.97</code> and Claude Engine <code>bf89abc</code> / <code>v6.17.0</code>. Two fictional messages and zero tool calls were persisted; the isolated runtime was cleaned after the run.</p>
    <a href={`${turn.media}/receipt.json`}>Inspect the selected proof receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
  </div></details>
</section>
<div class="voice-turn-next wrap"><p><strong>A separate local ordering example.</strong> The three synthetic notes below exercise multi-item ordering. The recorded voice turn above returned one actual speech chunk.</p></div>
<script>
  import { mountRecordedVoiceTurn } from '../showcases/voice-turn/controller';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-recorded-voice-turn]').forEach(mountRecordedVoiceTurn);
</script>
<style>
.voice-turn-next{padding-top:28px}.voice-turn-next p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);max-width:900px}.voice-turn-next strong{color:var(--ink)}.voice-turn-showcase{padding-block:24px 46px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:28px}.voice-turn-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;align-items:end;gap:24px 48px;margin-bottom:22px}.voice-turn-intro .eyebrow{font-size:14px;color:var(--rust);margin-bottom:14px}.voice-turn-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.3rem,4.5vw,4.1rem);line-height:1.08}.voice-turn-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.voice-turn-intro>p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);max-width:480px}.voice-turn-static{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;padding:15px 20px;background:#e9eddf;border-left:3px solid var(--forest);margin-bottom:24px}.voice-turn-clips{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}.voice-turn-clips article{min-width:0;padding:26px;background:#faf8f1;border:1px solid #a9b49e;border-radius:4px}.voice-turn-label{font-size:14px;color:var(--forest);margin-bottom:14px}.voice-turn-clips h3{font-size:27px;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:12px}.voice-turn-origin{font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted);min-height:52px}.voice-turn-clips audio{display:block;width:100%;min-width:0;margin:20px 0 24px}.voice-turn-transcript-label{font-size:14px;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:8px}.voice-turn-clips blockquote{padding:0;margin:0;border:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.75;font-family:var(--serif)}.voice-turn-result{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.voice-turn-path{max-width:920px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;padding:23px 0 26px}.voice-turn-disclosure{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.voice-turn-disclosure:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.voice-turn-disclosure>summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;min-height:56px;padding:14px 8px;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}.voice-turn-disclosure>summary :global(.ui-icon){flex-shrink:0}.voice-turn-disclosure[open]>summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.voice-turn-disclosure>div{padding:8px 0 22px}.voice-turn-disclosure figure{margin:0}.voice-turn-disclosure video{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1280/900;background:#111b25;border:1px solid #899281;border-radius:4px}.voice-turn-disclosure video::cue{font-size:clamp(14px,1.6vw,24px);background:#111b25;color:#fff}.voice-turn-disclosure figcaption,.voice-turn-method p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted);max-width:920px;margin-top:15px}.voice-turn-method p{margin:0 0 15px}.voice-turn-method code{font-size:14px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.voice-turn-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 28px;margin-top:10px}.voice-turn-links a,.voice-turn-method>a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:46px;font-size:15px;padding-block:8px}.voice-turn-showcase :is(audio,video,summary,a):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:5px}
@media(max-width:760px){.voice-turn-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.voice-turn-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,8vw,3.1rem)}.voice-turn-intro>p{font-size:16px}.voice-turn-clips{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}.voice-turn-clips article{padding:22px}.voice-turn-origin{min-height:0}.voice-turn-clips h3{font-size:26px}.voice-turn-static{padding:13px 16px}.voice-turn-disclosure video:not(:fullscreen)::cue{font-size:14px}.voice-turn-disclosure>summary{font-size:15px}.voice-turn-links{gap:0 20px}.voice-turn-showcase{padding-block:12px 34px}}
@media(max-width:380px){.voice-turn-clips article{padding:18px}.voice-turn-clips blockquote{font-size:18px}.voice-turn-clips h3{font-size:24px}}
</style>
